commit 0000000000000000000000000000000000000003
Author: Alessandro Carminati <alessandro.carminati@gmail.com>
Date:   Mon Oct 27 00:00:00 2026 +0100

    uaf_demo: use-after-free / double-free demonstrator

    Reproduces slide 13 of "Prague 2026 - OSS" using plain kmalloc()/kfree()
    on the shared kmalloc-512 slab - the real allocator path - so the fault
    is genuine, not staged in a private cache.

    The faulty Component A/B/C sequence runs on demand, the first time
    /dev/fake1 or /dev/fake2 is opened, and each allocator operation prints
    one kernel line:

        [A] alloc        obj=...
        [A] free         obj=...
        [B] fake1 alloc  obj=...
        [A] double free  obj=...
        [C] fake2 alloc  obj=...

    Because of SLUB's LIFO freelist the double free makes fake1 (B) and
    fake2 (C) alias the same object: a write through fake1 is then visible
    when reading fake2. This performs a real double free on the shared slab
    and is a demonstrator for an isolated VM only. Built into the kernel
    (CONFIG_UAF_DEMO=y, bool default y).

    fops are minimal: open, release, read, write.

    Signed-off-by: Alessandro Carminati <alessandro.carminati@gmail.com>

